Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.08,0:00:06.22,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Noah!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.81,0:00:13.44,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,It's just like Leviathan!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.96,0:00:15.86,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,So there were others?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.29,0:00:21.75,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,You have your own will, \Ntoo, don't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.75,0:00:22.70,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,In that case...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.98,0:00:26.41,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Obey me!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.85,0:00:46.06,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs32\t(0,2210,\fs33)\bord1.5\blur1.5\shad4\fnTimes New Roman\b1\c&HFEFDFF&\3c&HAD8261&\4c&H3F3936&\move(144,184,132,184,0,2196)}Fire
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.85,0:00:46.06,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs32\t(0,2210,\fs33)\bord1.5\blur1.5\shad4\fnTimes New Roman\b1\c&HFEFDFF&\3c&HAD8261&\4c&H3F3936&\move(144,320,132,330,0,2196)}Water
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.44,0:00:46.05,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Are you all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.65,0:00:49.53,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,You tamed it?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.53,0:00:50.45,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.03,0:00:54.07,Default,Cruz,0,0,0,,What? So quickly?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.07,0:00:56.08,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I should have known.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.07,0:01:00.18,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,What brilliant judgment.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.83,0:01:04.68,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,You chose Luthier without \Nthe slightest hesitation.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.68,0:01:06.27,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Luthier...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.27,0:01:09.23,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,It seems to possess a \Ngreat deal of power.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.23,0:01:12.80,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Would you like to test it? \NI will prepare a target.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.80,0:01:15.45,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,No, that won't be necessary.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.45,0:01:19.08,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Oh? Your eyes tell me you \Nhave some sort of plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.94,0:01:24.48,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Now, here I go.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.28,0:01:32.40,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Noah...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.40,0:01:33.58,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,It's all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.60,0:01:43.11,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Just as I predicted.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.11,0:01:46.03,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Leviathan is just slightly more powerful.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.33,0:01:49.02,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,It doesn't feel hot...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.02,0:01:50.95,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Look at the ground.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.07,0:01:56.42,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Leviathan is keeping it in check \Nto prevent the heat from escaping.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.42,0:01:59.95,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,You've tamed it to that point \Nalready? Astounding...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.95,0:02:03.03,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I formally entrust Luthier to you, Noah.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.03,0:02:07.47,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Use it for the good of the empire.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.47,0:02:08.52,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I shall.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:24.60,0:02:26.54,sign_generic,Title,0,0,0,,{\fade(109,0)\c&H4F7C81&\bord0\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs10\pos(320,142.5)}Born Blessed, So I'll Obtain Ultimate Power
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.60,0:02:26.54,sign_generic,Title,0,0,0,,{\fade(109,0)\p1\bord2\c&H291505&\alpha&H255&\3c&H2986A5&\fscx87\pos(311,141.167)}m 0 0 l 235 0 l 225 8 l 235 15 l 18 15 l 30 8 l 18 0
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.71,0:03:45.10,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,The Meeres Empire holds dominion \Nover a vast amount of land.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.10,0:03:50.46,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,Its highest ruler, the emperor, \Ngoverns all of its affairs.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.46,0:03:53.41,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,This includes domestic affairs, \Nsuch as law and finance,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.41,0:03:58.26,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,and diplomatic affairs, such as mediating\Ndisputes and international negotiations.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.83,0:04:04.63,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,The emperor also mediates in the \Nimperial family's private matters,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.63,0:04:08.64,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,known as internal law \Nand internal affairs.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.30,0:04:14.09,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,A personal declaration from the emperor's \Nyounger brother, Graeme Ararat?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.73,0:04:18.83,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Graeme's son... my nephew.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.83,0:04:22.20,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,He ruled over his domain \Nwith extreme tyranny,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.20,0:04:26.70,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,and now, in a drunken stupor,\Nkilled someone during an argument.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.70,0:04:30.07,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,That alone is a serious crime,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.07,0:04:34.60,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,but his father, Graeme, has declared \Na lack of oversight on his part
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.60,0:04:37.59,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,and personally offered to pay a fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.01,0:04:42.26,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Unfortunately, under imperial law, \NPrince Graeme has committed no crime.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.35,0:04:46.60,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Just as a child is not responsible \Nfor paying his parents' debts,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.96,0:04:49.81,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,a parent is not responsible \Nfor his child's crimes.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.23,0:04:52.18,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I said as much.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.18,0:04:55.41,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I suppose he's hoping \Nto buy peace of mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.41,0:04:57.00,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Thirty thousand rean...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.61,0:05:01.21,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,That's about 250 times the average \Nyearly income in the capital.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.21,0:05:02.94,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,It's a significant sum.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.45,0:05:05.98,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,What do you think, Noah?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.27,0:05:09.76,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,We cannot collect a fine from someone \Nwho has committed no crime.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.19,0:05:13.12,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Even if he has offered to pay it himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.45,0:05:16.05,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Then shall we revise the law
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.05,0:05:20.46,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,to institutionalize voluntary \Npayment of fines?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.46,0:05:24.05,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,The national treasury is \Nin chronic dire straits.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.05,0:05:29.72,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Disaster relief and suppression \Nof revolts do cost money.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.72,0:05:33.79,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,So that's why he's hoping to bring \Nin incidental income like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.23,0:05:35.94,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I can't blame him, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.74,0:05:39.00,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,If we were to set such a precedent,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.00,0:05:44.03,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,people would get the idea that they can \Nget out of any crime just by paying money.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.64,0:05:48.86,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,That would make the prevention \Nof crime more difficult.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.35,0:05:52.85,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,And since only the wealthy \Nwould be able to afford the fines—
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.85,0:05:55.79,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,major merchants, nobles, and \Ngovernment officials—
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.79,0:05:59.57,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,it would eventually breed \Ncorruption in our government.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.41,0:06:04.19,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,The empire's lack of funds \Nis a grave problem,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.19,0:06:08.71,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,but it is one we should resolve \Nthrough respectable means.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.11,0:06:13.62,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,True. You were right to admonish me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.38,0:06:28.96,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,To celebrate your wisdom, the likes \Nof which we rarely see in a ruler,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.96,0:06:31.87,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I hereby name you my premier advisor.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.87,0:06:33.05,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Advisor?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.05,0:06:34.56,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,It's an honorary post.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.56,0:06:36.13,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,You dislike it?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.19,0:06:41.00,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, I have a proposal.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.00,0:06:43.50,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Why not allow people to pay money
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.50,0:06:46.64,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,not to escape punishment, \Nbut to attain honor?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.20,0:06:52.08,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,For example, those who donate \Na thousand rean to the empire
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.08,0:06:55.05,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,may be granted honorary knighthood.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.95,0:07:00.21,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,It will need caveats to ensure it \Ncan't be abused to gain real power,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.21,0:07:05.03,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,but many would love to be granted such \Nan honor by Your Majesty personally.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.56,0:07:06.99,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,When humans...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.73,0:07:11.35,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,come into possession of more \Nmoney than they can use,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.79,0:07:15.08,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,they begin to desire honor more \Nthan physical possessions.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.40,0:07:18.89,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I see. What a brilliant idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.89,0:07:20.41,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,You impress me, Noah.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.41,0:07:23.87,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Cruz, summon Oscar. At once.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.87,0:07:24.75,Default,Cruz,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.75,0:07:25.71,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.55,0:07:30.79,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I've just remembered some unfinished \Nbusiness at the Ministry of Law.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.79,0:07:33.18,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Please allow me to take my leave.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.18,0:07:34.47,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,This needs to stop.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.95,0:07:39.13,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,If it goes any further, I'll be \Nintruding on Oscar's dominion.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.13,0:07:41.82,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,You are clever, Noah.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.10,0:07:51.85,Default,Sheezu,0,0,0,,They are all astonished by the \Namazing feat you've performed.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.85,0:07:53.19,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Oh, it's you, Sheezu.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.19,0:07:58.31,Default,Sheezu,0,0,0,,They can't comprehend how the ground \Ncould simply melt away like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.31,0:08:01.75,Default,Sheezu,0,0,0,,Someone has fallen into \Nit trying to find out.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.23,0:08:03.95,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,How careless.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.52,0:08:06.63,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Here.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.63,0:08:09.52,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,To treat the one who fell.\NSpare no expense.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.52,0:08:11.40,Default,Sheezu,0,0,0,,Thank you, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.40,0:08:12.34,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,And this?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.34,0:08:13.56,Default,Sheezu,0,0,0,,Ah.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.89,0:08:17.84,Default,Sheezu,0,0,0,,Something I had delivered \Nfor the Sixteenth Prince.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.84,0:08:19.87,Default,Sheezu,0,0,0,,He is only three,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.87,0:08:22.71,Default,Sheezu,0,0,0,,and he likes to make \Nrhinoceros beetles fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.33,0:08:24.66,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Huh...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.60,0:08:29.84,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Making them fight, eh?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.63,0:08:31.94,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Are you up to it?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.33,0:08:40.00,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Leviathan. Luthier.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.94,0:08:49.66,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,They really do have
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.66,0:08:52.90,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,all the techniques of their \Npast owners engraved in them.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.69,0:08:56.46,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I'm learning a lot watching them, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.67,0:09:00.95,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,The difference in strength is clear.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.95,0:09:02.73,Default,Gigi,0,0,0,,Wow!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.86,0:09:07.01,Default,Gigi,0,0,0,,Oh! Please pardon my intrusion!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.01,0:09:08.79,Default,Gigi,0,0,0,,That was magic, wasn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.79,0:09:10.30,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Want to see it again?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.30,0:09:11.52,Default,Gigi,0,0,0,,May I?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.52,0:09:13.42,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,They seem up for it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.82,0:09:19.17,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Unlike my faithful Leviathan,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.17,0:09:21.49,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Luthier seems quite competitive.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.90,0:09:29.29,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Learning their moves like this \Nmight make me stronger, too.
Dialogue: 1,0:09:30.50,0:09:34.46,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(862,0)\an7\fs14\fnTimes New Roman\c&HFFFCF4&\3c&HCDAFA0&\bord0.75\blur1\b1\shad1\4c&H7D605F&\pos(14,20)}Name: Minister-Prince of Justice Noah Ararat \NSex: Male \NLevel: 2\h/\h∞
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.50,0:09:34.46,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(862,0)\an7\bord2\shad2\blur1\p1\fscy220\alpha&H50&\c&H70858F&\3c&HF8D6AE&\4c&HB7775D&}m 0 0 l 258 0 258 21 0 21
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.25,0:09:34.46,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,My level went up!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.46,0:09:35.70,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Could it be...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.34,0:09:42.69,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Leviathan has won every \Nbattle so far, but now...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.84,0:09:49.86,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Well done. You've come into your own.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.86,0:09:56.32,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\c&HFCFDFC&\3c&HBB997E&\4c&H643F2D&\b1\fnTimes New Roman\bord0.75\blur1.5\shad5\move(206,35,206,137,0,5460)}Fire
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.86,0:09:56.32,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\c&HFCFDFC&\3c&HBB997E&\4c&H643F2D&\b1\fnTimes New Roman\bord0.75\blur1.5\shad5\move(206,120,206,225,0,5460)}Water
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.86,0:09:56.32,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\c&HFCFDFC&\3c&HBB997E&\4c&H5A463B&\b1\fnTimes New Roman\bord0.75\blur1.5\shad5\move(206,210,206,315,0,5460)}Wind
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.86,0:09:56.32,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\c&HFCFDFC&\3c&HBB997E&\4c&H41362D&\b1\fnTimes New Roman\bord0.75\blur1.5\shad5\move(206,295,206,397,0,5460)}Earth
Dialogue: 1,0:09:51.19,0:09:55.29,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,With Luthier's growth, the plus \Non my fire stat has gone up.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.29,0:09:56.31,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,And...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.61,0:09:57.48,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Zoey.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.48,0:09:58.80,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.21,0:10:02.36,top,Zoey,0,0,0,,By the power of the spirits with \Nwhom I have forged a pact,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.64,0:10:02.69,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,In the six years since I hired her,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.36,0:10:05.04,top,Zoey,0,0,0,,tell me this individual's \Nintentions and disposition.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.69,0:10:07.28,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Zoey has learned many skills to repay \Nthe debt she feels she owes me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.80,0:10:09.75,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,It went up.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.77,0:10:12.75,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\b1\an1\move(100,10,100,227)\bord0.5\shad5\fnTimes New Roman\blur1\fs40\c&HFFFCF5&\3c&HD1A98F&\4c&H8F5F4C&\frx24\fry352}Level
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.75,0:10:15.82,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,Amazing! You didn't even \Nhave to do any fighting!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.82,0:10:18.32,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,I've never heard of anything like this!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.32,0:10:20.66,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,This is the result of \Nmaking my dolls battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.07,0:10:25.52,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,S-So if you keep making them fight, \Nwill it keep going up forever?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.84,0:10:28.36,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,It isn't that simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.36,0:10:31.56,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,To raise it from Level 1 to 2 \Ntook only one battle,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.56,0:10:36.14,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,but to raise it from 2 to 3, I had \Nto make them fight over ten times.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.65,0:10:40.50,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I think fighting the same opponent \Nevery time is inefficient.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.50,0:10:41.95,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,Ah, I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.35,0:10:45.86,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,If I want to learn how it \Nworks in better detail,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.86,0:10:50.21,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I'll need to collect even \Nmore magic items like these.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.60,0:10:52.52,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,Now that sounds interesting.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.67,0:10:59.32,nameplate,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(272,477)\pos(602,264)\c&HEBEFEF&\3c&H564240&}Henry Ararat \N{\fs13}Minister-Prince of Military Affairs, Fourth Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.12,0:11:01.32,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.23,0:11:04.22,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,Making your magic sword battle your ring?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.22,0:11:06.22,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,That's the inventiveness I expect of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.51,0:11:08.64,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Where were you watching from?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.19,0:11:18.08,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,The monster nest has finally matured.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.51,0:11:21.16,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,It's time for your first campaign.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.16,0:11:22.73,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,The monster nest...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.29,0:11:26.45,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,A hunting ground managed by the \NMinistry of Military Affairs
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.45,0:11:29.46,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,for the purpose of serving as \Nevery prince's first campaign.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.76,0:11:31.68,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,When you open this box,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.68,0:11:35.69,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,it'll give a reading of how many soldiers \Nyou should take on your first campaign.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.69,0:11:37.17,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,We have a system for that?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.63,0:11:40.83,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,You don't want too many or too \Nfew for this sort of thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.29,0:11:42.93,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,Go on, open it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.26,0:11:51.66,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,One?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.66,0:11:55.24,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Does that mean I alone am sufficient?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.24,0:11:58.86,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,I don't believe it... \NThis is unprecedented.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.07,0:12:04.59,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,You really are amazing, you know that?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.61,0:12:07.93,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,Pardon me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.68,0:12:12.31,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,You have a visitor.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.84,0:12:15.45,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,He says he brings orders \Nfrom His Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.46,0:12:18.52,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Let him in.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.30,0:12:22.92,nameplate,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an1\fade(272,477)\c&HFAFEFF&\3c&H393F48&\pos(427.667,266)}Reiss Keiki \N{\fs12}Direct Subordinate of the Fourth Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.05,0:12:21.12,Default,Reiss,0,0,0,,Emperor's orders.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.84,0:12:25.05,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.05,0:12:27.10,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Someone who delivers a personal order
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.10,0:12:29.15,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,from the emperor can be\Nconsidered his proxy.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.15,0:12:33.22,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,He must be shown the same courtesy \Nas the emperor in every aspect.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.59,0:12:38.31,Default,Reiss,0,0,0,,Wise Prince Noah Ararat's first \Ncampaign will be postponed.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.31,0:12:40.49,Default,Reiss,0,0,0,,Stand by until you \Nreceive further orders.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.49,0:12:42.08,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.14,0:12:46.44,Default,Reiss,0,0,0,,It is good to see you \Nagain, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.81,0:12:52.69,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Oh, right. Reiss. You are \Npart of Henry's household.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.69,0:12:53.73,Default,Reiss,0,0,0,,I am.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.21,0:12:56.18,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,Members of the imperial family
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.18,0:13:00.72,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,sometimes send one of their slaves or \Nservants away to serve as officials.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.16,0:13:03.30,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,Those of such origins are considered
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.30,0:13:08.55,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,members of that noble's family who have \Nbeen discharged from their service.
Dialogue: 1,0:13:09.76,0:13:13.34,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,They are considered government officials\Nand subordinates of the imperial family.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.97,0:13:20.77,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(781,0)\fnTimes New Roman\c&H2B3B41&\fs15\bord0\pos(249.333,59.333)}Noah
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.97,0:13:20.77,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(781,0)\fnTimes New Roman\c&H2B3B41&\fs15\bord0\pos(368,59.333)}Henry
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.97,0:13:20.77,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(781,0)\fnTimes New Roman\c&H12242F&\fs15\bord0\pos(262.667,112.667)}Imperial Family
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.97,0:13:20.77,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\b1\fade(781,0)\fnTimes New Roman\c&H2B3B41&\fs10\bord0.5\pos(359.334,108.001)\3c&HB7D6DE&}Household\NMember
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.97,0:13:20.77,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\b1\fade(781,0)\fnTimes New Roman\c&H2B3B41&\fs10\bord0.5\3c&HC5E2E9&\pos(296.668,188.667)}Subordinate
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.97,0:13:20.77,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs15\fade(781,0)\fnTimes New Roman\c&H2B3B41&\bord0\pos(312.667,282)}Reiss
Dialogue: 1,0:13:13.71,0:13:16.96,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,The imperial household members who \Nwork in service to each prince
Dialogue: 1,0:13:16.96,0:13:19.98,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,have the strictest etiquette \Nstandards imposed on them.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.32,0:13:23.77,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Why has it been postponed?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.77,0:13:26.21,Default,Reiss,0,0,0,,Entirely because of your strength.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.21,0:13:30.09,Default,Reiss,0,0,0,,The emperor was so delighted \Nby the unprecedented reading,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.09,0:13:33.65,Default,Reiss,0,0,0,,he said it should be \Ncarried out on a grand scale.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.65,0:13:35.47,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,So that explains it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.86,0:13:40.58,Default,Reiss,0,0,0,,His Majesty is currently working with \NPrince Henry and the Eighth Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.58,0:13:44.81,Default,Reiss,0,0,0,,to come up with a way to share how \Nremarkable you are with the whole empire.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.23,0:13:49.17,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Then I guess my first campaign \Nwon't happen for a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.17,0:13:52.64,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,Magic items that possess their own will?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.64,0:13:53.78,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.78,0:13:55.14,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Anything will suffice.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.14,0:13:57.80,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Something like a cursed doll,\Nfor example.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.80,0:14:01.57,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,I'm terribly sorry.\NI don't have anything like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.57,0:14:02.96,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.96,0:14:05.83,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Well, I didn't expect to \Nfind more right away.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.23,0:14:07.69,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Shirley, if you please.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.29,0:14:09.83,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,R-Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.04,0:14:12.28,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Take this.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.77,0:14:15.40,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,If you come across anything that \Nmight fit the bill, contact me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.40,0:14:17.66,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,B-But... I can't accept that!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.66,0:14:22.55,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Oh, and of course, I'll reward you \Nagain if you find anything good.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.46,0:14:24.56,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I'm counting on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.83,0:14:30.98,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,Th-Thank you so much!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.05,0:14:33.39,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.08,0:14:35.56,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,I'm very sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.56,0:14:39.44,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,I just can't believe you paid him so \Nmuch when he didn't have anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.44,0:14:41.89,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,That's how nobles shop.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.83,0:14:43.11,top,Dalem,0,0,0,,Do you even know who I am?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.12,0:14:46.57,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,Say that again if you think you can!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.57,0:14:48.01,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,What did you say?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.01,0:14:52.31,Default,Shopkeeper,0,0,0,,I said that another customer has \Nalready reserved that item...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.31,0:14:55.30,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,And I'm telling you that {\i1}I'll{\i0} buy it!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.28,0:15:00.72,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,Hey, what's with those looks?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.72,0:15:03.39,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,You guys all do business \Nhere too, don't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.39,0:15:06.27,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,You want to lose your deals with us?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.27,0:15:07.28,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Stop.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.41,0:15:10.59,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,Huh?! Who the hell are—
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.14,0:15:15.71,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,Well, if it isn't Prince Noah!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.71,0:15:17.26,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,You know me?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.26,0:15:18.95,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,Allow me to introduce myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.95,0:15:21.38,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,I am a member of\NPrince Gilbert's household.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.38,0:15:23.30,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,My name is Dalem.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.80,0:15:27.21,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,I once saw you at the Ministry \Nof the Imperial Household.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.21,0:15:29.60,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,And why is a man like you doing this?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.60,0:15:31.20,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,That was intimidation.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.20,0:15:32.98,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,What's this now?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.98,0:15:37.37,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,You are the minister-prince of \Njustice, and you don't know?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.99,0:15:40.75,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,Those in the Ministry of the Imperial \NHousehold can't be found guilty
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.75,0:15:43.56,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,of any crimes other than insurrection \Nor assisting an enemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.56,0:15:46.88,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,I am quite familiar with \Nimperial law myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.15,0:15:50.78,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,So I would rather you \Ndidn't say anything to me,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.78,0:15:53.39,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,no matter how trifling it may be.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.65,0:15:57.14,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,Prince Noah?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.14,0:16:00.61,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Servants of the imperial family,\Nespecially princes,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.61,0:16:02.42,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,already enjoy quite high status.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.83,0:16:05.18,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,And he's a member of the \NFirst Prince's household
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.18,0:16:07.66,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,{\i0}and{\i1} the Ministry of the \NImperial Household.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.06,0:16:10.71,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,He's privileged enough that his \Nattitude isn't surprising.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.73,0:16:13.74,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I understand clearly.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.16,0:16:14.98,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.98,0:16:17.96,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,But? But what?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.96,0:16:20.99,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,You said you are a member \Nof my brother's household.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.99,0:16:24.58,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,If so, why are you standing up \Nstraight when you look at me?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.98,0:16:28.33,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,It's the same as when \NI saw Reiss yesterday.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.69,0:16:32.81,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Based on our positions, Dalem \Nshould be showing respect to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.81,0:16:34.06,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,I-I didn't realize—
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.06,0:16:36.12,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Too late. Apprehend him, Shirley!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.12,0:16:36.67,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,Right away!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.19,0:16:46.52,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,But I am Prince Gilbert's...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.52,0:16:47.55,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Silence.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.10,0:16:51.48,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,You still don't understand that \Nyou've tarnished my brother's name?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.11,0:16:54.60,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Dalem, part of the First \NPrince's household,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.60,0:16:56.93,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,has behaved rudely toward \Nthe Thirteenth Prince.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.35,0:16:59.42,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,He will be punished under internal law.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.88,0:17:01.12,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Who has a whip?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.46,0:17:02.50,Default,Onlooker,0,0,0,,I do!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.49,0:17:06.00,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,Why are you people just watching?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.00,0:17:09.33,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,You'll regret this, damn it!\NI swear you will!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.33,0:17:11.05,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,I'll make sure you pay!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.50,0:17:13.64,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,I am of the Ministry of \Nthe Imperial Household!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.89,0:17:15.48,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,How many lashes?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.88,0:17:17.07,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Well, let's see...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.60,0:17:19.01,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,If you or one of my household
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.01,0:17:22.10,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,tyrannized my people under the\Nmantle of borrowed authority,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.39,0:17:24.95,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I wouldn't hesitate to \Nsentence you to death.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.25,0:17:29.69,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.43,0:17:32.55,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,Y-Your Highness! Please forgive me!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.73,0:17:33.38,top,OnlookerA,0,0,0,,Serves you right!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.38,0:17:35.13,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,Please forgive me, Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.20,0:17:36.87,top,OnlookerB,0,0,0,,All you ever did was throw your \Nweight around to screw us over!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.87,0:17:39.05,Default,Dalem,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.39,0:17:49.92,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,He has breathed his last.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.92,0:17:52.97,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,All right. Has law enforcement arrived?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.97,0:17:53.94,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.94,0:17:56.78,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Once all is taken care of, \Nhave them write a report
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.78,0:17:58.68,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,with the charges I described earlier.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.68,0:18:00.21,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.21,0:18:03.18,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Also, get me a set of handcuffs.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.18,0:18:04.14,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.76,0:18:12.24,Default,Guard,0,0,0,,Oh, if it isn't the Thirteenth Prince...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.24,0:18:13.16,Default,Guard,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.83,0:18:16.87,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I've come to apologize to my brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.87,0:18:18.41,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Would you tell him that, please?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.81,0:18:21.32,Default,Coil,0,0,0,,Let him in.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.58,0:18:24.97,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,Who is that man?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.97,0:18:26.52,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,His butler, Coil.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.36,0:18:30.54,Default,Coil,0,0,0,,Please enter. Prince Gilbert awaits.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.11,0:18:37.92,sign_generic,EPTitle,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\b1\fade(522,721)\c&H00070B&\pos(320, 205)}Episode 8
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.11,0:18:37.92,sign_generic,EPTitle,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\b1\fade(522,721)\c&H00070B&\pos(320, 225)}The First Versus the Thirteenth
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.55,0:18:44.55,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,I see. Well, there was no \Nother way to handle it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.16,0:18:49.10,top,Gilbert,0,0,0,,A mere member of my household dared \Nto disparage an imperial prince.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.76,0:18:49.85,nameplate,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(272,477)\c&HF7FBFB&\3c&H5C5C5C&\pos(253,262)}Gilbert Ararat \N{\fs13}First Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.10,0:18:51.15,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,He deserved death.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.48,0:18:55.24,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Still, I should have \Nconsulted with you first.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.56,0:18:57.20,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I sincerely apologize.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.68,0:19:02.94,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,But... Dalem... Dalem, you say?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.94,0:19:04.49,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,I don't remember that name.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.82,0:19:06.37,Default,Coil,0,0,0,,If I may...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.37,0:19:09.62,Default,Coil,0,0,0,,He relocated to the Ministry of the \NImperial Household a few years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.62,0:19:11.96,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,Oh, right, him.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.96,0:19:15.04,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,All the more reason not \Nto fret over this.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.04,0:19:19.68,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,I fired him and sent him \Naway for misconduct.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.68,0:19:22.25,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,He couldn't even be called \Na member of my household.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.25,0:19:23.82,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I see. So that's it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.47,0:19:34.43,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,In fact, I would even go so far as \Nto say you protected my reputation.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.43,0:19:37.30,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,Had he been left to his \Nown devices any longer,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.30,0:19:41.93,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,he would have continued to carry \Nout evil deeds in my name.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.19,0:19:44.99,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Thank you, dear brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.29,0:19:50.67,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,But I can see why His Majesty \Nnamed you the keeper of the law.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.67,0:19:55.07,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,Most wouldn't have carried out his \Nsentence on the spot like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.28,0:19:59.01,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,Um, Prince Noah...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.01,0:20:02.70,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,What was the purpose of that apology?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.70,0:20:03.51,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Hmm?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.14,0:20:06.02,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,Well, you see...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.02,0:20:08.92,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,You're asking if it was necessary \Nto go see him in handcuffs
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.92,0:20:12.13,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,when he seemed so nonchalant \Nabout the whole thing?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.13,0:20:14.27,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,Oh... Yes, exactly!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.27,0:20:17.12,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Despite how he looked, he was furious.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.06,0:20:21.90,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,But he couldn't afford to create \Na rift between him and me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.54,0:20:26.47,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,The emperor favors me more than \Nhim right now, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.47,0:20:28.03,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,Oh...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.51,0:20:32.00,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,If the younger brother apologizes \Nfirst after doing something wrong,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.43,0:20:34.30,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,what does the older brother do?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.30,0:20:37.01,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,Oh, that I can understand!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.01,0:20:39.92,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,He can't get mad if the younger \Nbrother apologizes first.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.43,0:20:45.45,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Not to mention my brother disavowed Dalem\Nand the slave traders with such ease.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.96,0:20:50.73,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,If I'd done nothing, I'd become \Na target for harassment.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.23,0:20:53.90,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Behind the curtain,\Nhe sees me as an enemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.90,0:20:58.04,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I apologized, and he accepted it.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.84,0:21:03.42,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Among nobles, rehashing a problem\Npreviously apologized for is unseemly.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.29,0:21:06.20,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,You gave it {\i1}that{\i0} much thought?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.12,0:21:08.11,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,Incredible!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.07,0:21:13.03,Default,Dylan,0,0,0,,Prince Noah, you have a visitor.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.03,0:21:16.33,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,You're the one showing \Nthem in? How unusual.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.64,0:21:19.30,Default,Dylan,0,0,0,,He says he's from the Ministry \Nof the Imperial Household.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.86,0:21:20.93,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.36,0:21:24.34,Default,Don,0,0,0,,It's an honor to meet you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.34,0:21:27.34,Default,Don,0,0,0,,My name is Don Orts.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.34,0:21:28.76,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,What do you want?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.76,0:21:33.57,Default,Don,0,0,0,,I was deeply impressed by how you \Nhandled yesterday's incident.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.57,0:21:39.35,Default,Don,0,0,0,,I have come to ask that you allow \Nme to work under you as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.71,0:21:43.17,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Me? But our jurisdictions are different.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.17,0:21:46.45,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,A member of the Ministry of the Imperial\NHousehold would struggle here.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.30,0:21:48.95,Default,Don,0,0,0,,I don't mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.95,0:21:51.92,Default,Don,0,0,0,,You can simply use me \Nwhenever you have the need.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.36,0:21:54.67,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.97,0:21:57.49,Default,Don,0,0,0,,Thank you!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.09,0:22:03.96,Default,Dylan,0,0,0,,Dylan.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.96,0:22:04.95,Default,Dylan,0,0,0,,Yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.79,0:22:07.97,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Look into that man.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.97,0:22:09.93,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,And be thorough about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:11.45,0:22:12.97,sign_generic,Credits,0,0,0,,{\an3\fade(443,0)\fnTimes New Roman\b1\c&HC3D0DD&\3c&H374B69&\blur1\bord1.5\fs10\pos(302.667,258.667)}Translation:\NTiming:\NEditing:\NQuality Control:
